    {
      "id": "roMz7iePn6OjA4f5bOjEL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -161.1602783203125,
      "y": 5063.899921417236,
      "width": 975.0992431640625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ar",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1230575364,
      "version": 709,
      "versionNonce": 1516933692,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781288632555,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q. In a production grade application how do we decide on which column we will be creating index \nor whether we will create composite index?   \n        - No, perfect ans exist for this question\n        - Query patterns -> find which component of ur db is read heavy and queried the most\n        - What is the business requirement and based on that u decide how to query that.\n- In general, even after deciding what indexes to build, it's recommended that we properly test the \necosystem for performance. \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q. In a production grade application how do we decide on which column we will be creating index \nor whether we will create composite index?   \n        - No, perfect ans exist for this question\n        - Query patterns -> find which component of ur db is read heavy and queried the most\n        - What is the business requirement and based on that u decide how to query that.\n- In general, even after deciding what indexes to build, it's recommended that we properly test the \necosystem for performance. \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
