    {
      "id": "5twzJU6sREg6SBOwepyAa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -24.56024169921875,
      "y": 5723.49995803833,
      "width": 373.81976318359375,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b03",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 413900420,
      "version": 146,
      "versionNonce": 189334716,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781289526692,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "if there are n columns in ur db\n - max number of indexes u can make ?\n    - 2^n-1 => 2^n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "if there are n columns in ur db\n - max number of indexes u can make ?\n    - 2^n-1 => 2^n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Uo4IgfmJ-6vSLjzLRhUy_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -137.56024169921875,
      "y": 5834.699939727783,
      "width": 1233.5191650390625,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 440103172,
      "version": 1023,
      "versionNonce": 371030988,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781361156465,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "#Primary Index : clustered index\n         - There might be some order of data which is very crucial for us \n         - what if, we create an index that can determine the actual, real physical order of data on the disk.\n         -  array + bst =>>>> \n Consider the two cases: \n         - array of products which is unsorted then we a balanced binary search tree which keeps products sorted by price. \n         - array of products which are already sorted by category \n         - then there comes the concept of primary index entries points to direct physical order of the data\n    B-tree -> the primary index points directly to the actual location of data in the disk which is also sorted/arranged by the\n                 primary index order, works on top of primary key\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "#Primary Index : clustered index\n         - There might be some order of data which is very crucial for us \n         - what if, we create an index that can determine the actual, real physical order of data on the disk.\n         -  array + bst =>>>> \n Consider the two cases: \n         - array of products which is unsorted then we a balanced binary search tree which keeps products sorted by price. \n         - array of products which are already sorted by category \n         - then there comes the concept of primary index entries points to direct physical order of the data\n    B-tree -> the primary index points directly to the actual location of data in the disk which is also sorted/arranged by the\n                 primary index order, works on top of primary key\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
