      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781361413807,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hash Based index -> generate hash codes for each row on the indexed cols. Index contains pointers\nto the value rather than the entire value",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hash Based index -> generate hash codes for each row on the indexed cols. Index contains pointers\nto the value rather than the entire value",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Z1l4QKtW6FOGH8f1L11sV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -73.98038482666016,
      "y": 7165.499973297119,
      "width": 1082.2393798828125,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1906668916,
      "version": 548,
      "versionNonce": 1966529228,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781362709198,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Problem with Hash based index\n       - range queries and sorting criterias \n\n- Adaptive hash index  -> When mysql index sees some date getting queried very frequently then it can create \na hash index on top of btree index.\n\n- if ur table is already existing and if we create a new index, then in general most dbs, lock the table\n  when creating a new table\n\n# how to now add indexes in a spring boot driven backend application",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Problem with Hash based index\n       - range queries and sorting criterias \n\n- Adaptive hash index  -> When mysql index sees some date getting queried very frequently then it can create \na hash index on top of btree index.\n\n- if ur table is already existing and if we create a new index, then in general most dbs, lock the table\n  when creating a new table\n\n# how to now add indexes in a spring boot driven backend application",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
